The Roosevelt sits in the heart of Hollywood, and a short ride takes you into several vibrant neighboring cities. Below is a curated guide that combines the most‑visited, highest‑rated, and “must‑have‑fun” spots in each city, complete with practical details (address, hours, price, and a quick tip).  

---

## 1️⃣ Los Angeles – Hollywood & Central LA  
*The core of movie‑magic, iconic views, and historic nightlife.*

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Address | Hours (Typical) | Price / Ticket | Quick Tip |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|----------------|----------------|-----------|
| **A** | **Griffith Observatory** | Hill‑top city & Hollywood‑sign views; planetarium shows; easy hiking trails. | 2800 E Observatory Rd, Los Angeles, CA 90027 | Daily 10 am‑12 am (observatory closed 5‑7 pm) | Free entry; planetarium $7‑$9 | Arrive **30 min before sunset** for the best skyline photo. |
| **B** | **Hollywood Walk of Fame** | 2,600 brass stars honoring film, TV, music, radio & theater legends; street‑performers. | Hollywood Blvd, between La Brea Ave & Gower St | Open 24 h | Free | Pair with a **guided “Hollywood Legends” walking tour** ($≈25) for insider stories. |
| **C** | **TCL Chinese Theatre** | Historic cinema with celebrity hand‑prints, premiere events, and a dazzling marquee. | 6925 Hollywood Blvd, Los Angeles, CA 90028 | Tours 10 am‑5 pm (Mon‑Sat) | $15 adult | Book **online**; tours fill fast on weekends. |
| **D** | **Hollywood Museum** (Lloyd Wright Building) | Treasure‑trove of movie memorabilia, costumes, props, and original set pieces. | 1660 N Highland Ave, Los Angeles, CA 90028 | Tue‑Sun 10 am‑5 pm (closed Mon) | $15 adult / $12 senior / $10 student | Pair with a **Dolby Theatre** tour for a full Hollywood experience. |
| **E** | **Dolby Theatre (Oscars Venue)** | Backstage tours of the Academy Awards home; state‑of‑the‑art sound & lighting. | 6801 Hollywood Blvd, Los Angeles, CA 90028 | Tours 10 am‑5 pm (Mon‑Sat) | $25 adult / $20 senior / $15 student | **Reserve ahead**; tours sell out quickly. |
| **F** | **The Hollywood Roosevelt Rooftop Pool & Bar** | Historic pool where movie stars once swam; rooftop bar with city views. | 7000 Hollywood Blvd (hotel) | Pool 7 am‑10 pm (seasonal); Bar 5 pm‑midnight | Pool for hotel guests; drinks $12‑$18 | Ask for the **“Rooftop Sunset Cocktail”** – a house specialty. |

---

## 2️⃣ West Hollywood – Nightlife & Creative Vibe (≈ 5 mi)

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Address | Hours | Price |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|-------|-------|
| **G** | **Sunset Strip** | Legendary nightlife corridor with neon billboards, iconic music venues (The Roxy, Whisky A Go Go) and trendy restaurants. | Sunset Blvd, West Hollywood, CA 90069 | Open 24 h | Free to stroll (shows vary) |
| **H** | **The Comedy Store** | Live stand‑up from world‑renowned comedians; historic comedy venue. | 8432 Sunset Blvd, West Hollywood, CA 90069 | Shows 7 pm‑midnight (Fri‑Sat) | $20‑$30 per seat |
| **I** | **West Hollywood Design District** | Boutique shops, art galleries, street murals, specialty coffee spots. | Santa Monica Blvd & Melrose Ave | 10 am‑7 pm (shops) | Free |
| **J** | **Plummer Park** | Outdoor concerts, skate park, picnic areas; great for a relaxed afternoon. | 626 N Vista St, West Hollywood, CA 90069 | 6 am‑10 pm | Free |

*Evening tip:* After dinner on the Strip, catch a comedy show and finish with a nightcap at a rooftop bar in West Hollywood.

---

## 3️⃣ Burbank – Studio‑City Experience (≈ 13 mi)

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Address | Hours | Price |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|-------|-------|
| **K** | **Warner Bros. Studio Tour Hollywood** | Behind‑the‑scenes look at sound stages, iconic sets (e.g., “Friends” Central Perk), DC Universe props. | 400 Burbank Blvd, Burbank, CA 91502 | 8 am‑5 pm daily | $69 adult / $59 senior / $49 student |
| **L** | **Universal Studios Hollywood** (just over the border in Universal City) | Thrilling rides, “Wizarding World of Harry Potter,” live stunt shows. | 1000 Universal City Plaza, Universal City, CA 91608 | 8 am‑10 pm (seasonal) | $109‑$139 (one‑day) |
| **M** | **Burbank Town Center** | Shopping, dining, occasional street festivals; a convenient “break‑time” hub. | 250 E Magnolia Blvd, Burbank, CA 91502 | 10 am‑9 pm | Free |

*Best for movie‑buffs:* Combine the Warner Bros. tour with a quick lunch at the Town Center, then head to Universal Studios for an afternoon of thrills.

---

## 4️⃣ Glendale – Upscale Shopping & Neon Art (≈ 15 mi)

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Address | Hours | Price |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|-------|-------|
| **N** | **The Americana at Brand** | Upscale outdoor mall with a river‑fountain, live music, and a giant Christmas tree (winter). | 889 Americana Way, Glendale, CA 91210 | 10 am‑9 pm | Free (shopping/dining varies) |
| **O** | **Museum of Neon Art (MONA)** | Collection of vintage neon signs, kinetic art, and interactive installations. | 814 S Brand Blvd, Glendale, CA 91204 | Tue‑Sat 11 am‑5 pm | $10 adult |
| **P** | **Travel Town Museum** (near Glendale border) | Historic locomotives, mini‑railroad for kids, rail‑history exhibits. | 5200 N Hollywood Way, Los Angeles, CA 90027 | 10 am‑5 pm | $5 adult |

*Why Glendale stands out:* It offers a blend of high‑end retail, quirky neon art, and family‑friendly rail history—all within a short drive from the Roosevelt.

---

## 5️⃣ Santa Monica – Beach‑Side Fun (≈ 18 mi)

| # | Attraction | Why It’s Fun | Address | Hours | Price |
|---|------------|--------------|---------|-------|-------|
| **Q** | **Santa Monica Pier & Pacific Park** | Classic boardwalk with Ferris wheel, arcade, street performers, and ocean views. | 200 Santa Monica Pier, Santa Monica, CA 90401 | Pier 6 am‑10 pm; rides 11 am‑10 pm | Free entry; rides $5‑$10 |
| **R** | **Third Street Promenade** | Pedestrian‑only shopping street, cafés, and live street musicians. | 3rd St & Broadway, Santa Monica, CA 90401 | 10 am‑9 pm (shops) | Free |
| **S** | **Annenberg Community Beach House** | Historic pool, art exhibitions, rooftop deck with ocean vistas. | 415 Pacific Coast Hwy, Santa Monica, CA 90402 | 9 am‑5 pm (summer) | Free (parking $5) |
| **T** | **Palisades Park** | Cliff‑side walking path with sweeping ocean panoramas – perfect for sunset picnics. | Ocean Ave & Pacific Coast Hwy, Santa Monica, CA 90402 | Open 24 h | Free |

*Beach‑day tip:* Grab a quick bite at the Promenade, then head to the Pier for rides; finish with a sunset stroll along Palisades Park.

---

## 📅 Sample “One‑Day” Itinerary (maximizing fun & minimizing travel)

| Time | Activity | Location |
|------|----------|----------|
| **9:00 am** | Breakfast at **The Original Pantry Café** (classic LA diner) | 877 S Figueroa St, LA |
| **10:30 am** | Walk the **Hollywood Walk of Fame** & peek inside **TCL Chinese Theatre** | Hollywood Blvd |
| **12:00 pm** | Lunch at **Musso & Frank Grill** (historic Hollywood eatery) | 6667 Hollywood Blvd |
| **1:30 pm** | **Griffith Observatory** – planetarium show & short hike | 2800 E Observatory Rd |
| **4:00 pm** | Return to the Roosevelt, relax at the **Rooftop Pool** | The Hollywood Roosevelt |
| **5:30 pm** | Sunset cocktail on the **Rooftop Bar** | Same |
| **7:00 pm** | Dinner at **Pink Taco** (vibrant Mexican‑fusion) | 8000 Sunset Blvd (nearby) |
| **9:00 pm** | **Comedy Show** at **The Comedy Store** (West Hollywood) | 8432 Sunset Blvd |

*Feel free to swap the evening comedy for a night‑cap at the **Dolby Theatre** tour or a stroll along the **Sunset Strip**.*

---

## How to Use This Guide

1. **Pick a “base” city** – Los Angeles for classic Hollywood, West Hollywood for nightlife, Burbank for studio tours, Glendale for upscale shopping & neon art, or Santa Monica for beach fun.  
2. **Plan around opening hours** – most attractions open around 10 am; sunset spots (Griffith, Palisades, rooftop) shine between 5‑7 pm.  
3. **Bundle tickets** – many city‑pass packages (e.g., **Go Los Angeles Pass**) bundle the Hollywood Museum, Griffith Observatory, and a studio tour for a discount.  
4. **Transportation** – the Roosevelt is within walking distance of the **Hollywood/Highland Metro Red Line** station. Use **Metro Bus 704** (Hollywood Blvd) or rideshare for West Hollywood, Burbank, and Santa Monica.  

Enjoy your adventure around the iconic Hollywood Roosevelt – you’re right in the middle of LA’s most fun, photogenic, and unforgettable attractions!

